WEBVTT

00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:03.650
Her Majesty arrives!

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.840
So she's the Queen of the Witch World?

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.630
So hot!

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.340
Why is it so hot!?

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:01.090
Why aren't Hadzuki-chan and Ai-chan coming?

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:04.320
I can't stand this anymore!

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.970
Hey!

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:09.470
Stop being so loud, it's so hot...

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:12.070
It's summer, so of course it's hot!

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.310
Take your work more seriously!

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:17.740
Then please install an air conditioner for me.

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:19.040
That's too expensive.

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.480
You guys get cold drinks but I don't get anything.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:27.270
Please, buy an air conditioner.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.650
T-This music is...

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:41.140
All because you said something unnecessary, and now Dela's here!

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:44.010
I must hide, so tell her that I'm not here.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.020
It's too late.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.160
What?

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:59.950
~ That's mean, pretending that you're not here. ~

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.300
Oh, shut up!

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.620
I'm not installing an air conditioner!

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.170
Go home now!

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.540
My, how rude.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.080
I'm just here to give you something from Mota and Motamota.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.690
Give us something?

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.560
Aren't these Witch Apprentice Certificates?

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:18.590
Certificates?

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.630
You get these once you pass level 6.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.190
There is a magic sphere in there called a sphere of certification, which looks like any other magic sphere.

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:29.600
From now on, with every level that you pass, you will get such a sphere.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.350
Once you get eight of these, you will become a real witch.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.520
Oh, I see.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.960
You will need those starting from the next exam.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.490
You have to treasure them.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.440
Okay.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.990
Then let me give these to Hadzuki-chan and Ai-chan.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:47.500
Hey! W-Wait, Doremi!

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.080
If you're not here, who's going to look after the store!?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.110
Wow, that Ojamajo...

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:02.100
We are the Pureleine!

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.850
I am truly sorry.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:12.210
Lady Hadzuki went swimming at the school pool.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.850
She is not here right now.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:17.640
Today is a swimming day!

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.490
Use yer arms more!

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:24.860
Yes, like that! Jus' a bit more!

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.580
Hadzuki-chan, yer so close...

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.910
But Kanae-chan, yer a bit...

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.610
Ai-chan.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.210
Kanae-chan, try your best!

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.400
Yep.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.060
I guess...

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.530
Heeeeyyyy!

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:43.320
It's Doremi-chan. Why's she here now?

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:48.010
I forgot and went over to the Maho-dou!

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:52.290
I'm so sorry, but it ended 10 minutes ago.

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.730
Right now Ai-chan is teaching us how to exercise using the chin-up bars.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.640
Kanae-chan is here too.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.780
Yeah, since I'm not good at this.

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:07.000
I went home to get my swimsuit, so that's why I'm so late...

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.430
Are you okay?

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.120
What happened?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.660
Did she fall down from the bar?

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:13.300
Yes.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.520
I'll go get the teacher.

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:18.290
You twisted it.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:22.620
The bruise will go away in two or three days, so please don't use your foot too much.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.260
Okay.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:27.010
I already called your house, but no one answered.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:29.470
Mama is in the hospital right now.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.310
I see.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:31.980
This isn't good.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.930
But I still need to stay at school...

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:38.400
Yuki-sensei, we'll take her home.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.310
But wouldn't that trouble you?

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.640
We should help each other out in times like this.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:44.390
Doremi-chan.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.520
So hot...

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.940
I'm sorry, Ai-chan. I'm a bit heavy.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.390
That's fine...

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:53.780
But why am I the only one carryin' her?

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:57.960
I was running around all this time, so I'm out of energy.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.460
Go, Ai-chan.

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:04.130
Oh yeah, Kanae-chan, ya said that yer mom's in the hospital?

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.890
She got into a car accident a week ago.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:10.850
So I have to take her place and help out Papa at his restaurant.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:14.260
Kanae-chan's family runs a steakhouse, right?

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.060
Steak!?

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.070
Kanae-chan, your family owns a steakhouse!?

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:20.580
Kanae-chan's family's steak is really delicious.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:21.940
Really? Really!?

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.360
Kanae-chan, why didn't you tell me this sooner!?

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:28.500
It's not too late now.

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.390
Kanae-chan, be my best friend.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:31.780
W-What's with you, all of a sudden?

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:33.740
It's fine, it's fine.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.520
Ah, Ai-chan.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:38.240
I, her very best friend, will carry her from now on.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.250
Come, Kanae-chan. Hurry.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.200
O-Okay...

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.980
Kanae-chan, we are the bestest of friends, right?

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:47.670
Right?

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:51.020
She's too obvious, doing all this for steak.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:53.180
She's so simple.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.220
Papa, I'm home.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:56.570
Papa?

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.620
Kanae-chan, do you have a cat?

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:03.310
Nope.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.020
Am I hearing things?

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.200
Papa, what's wrong?

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.500
It's nothing, I just burned myself a little.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:13.570
You too?

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.540
No, it's really nothing.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.900
And, thank you all for bringing Kanae home in such hot weather.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:21.790
Now, drink up.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.750
Thank you for the drink!

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:27.170
It's so cold and delicious!

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.630
Juice can actually taste so good!

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:35.640
I'm sure your steak is really good too, right, right, Mister?

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:43.280
Oh yeah, yer mom got into a car accident, you twisted twisted yer foot, and yer dad burned his hand.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.810
That's a lotta accidents.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.460
10 days ago, a thief even broke in.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.740
Our business is also going down the drain.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.860
We're just out of luck.

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:55.200
The steak here is really good, but you're losing customers?

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:59.200
Yes. Ever since that thief broke in, our business has taken a turn for the worse.

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:03.580
Now that even Kanae is hurt, it looks like I can't keep this restaurant open any longer.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:06.420
Mister, let us help you out!

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:07.630
Really?

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.090
Then I need to properly thank you girls.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.590
Well, there's no need to thank me! Just give me steak!

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.440
Kanae-chan, please be my best friend forever!

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.430
You idiot!

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:24.750
But my best friend is really in a tight spot.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:26.730
How can I just leave her like that?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.480
Your face just reads, "I want to eat steak."

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:30.690
No way.

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:36.070
But Kanae-chan really is having some problems.

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:40.480
But who will look after the Maho-dou?

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:42.350
You just leave that to me!

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:45.750
Pop.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:49.140
I have many rich boyfriends.

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:51.960
Once I call them, they will buy up all our magic goods.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:54.840
You haven't even passed the level 9 exam...

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:57.830
No, I think she's more reliable than you.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:59.350
N-No way!

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:03.850
I get it. Well then, until that kid gets better, you can help out at that steakhouse.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:05.580
Really? Thank you.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:06.850
That's great, Doremi-chan.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:10.650
I feel a bit confused right now.

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:15.650
It's been an hour already! Why ain't anyone comin'!?

00:09:15.650 --> 00:09:18.100
Looks like this place really isn't popular.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.950
Welcome!

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:26.680
What's wrong?

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:29.130
Masa-kun, let's forget about this store.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.920
Eh? Why?

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:32.220
Let's just go.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:33.340
Hey.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.150
Hey, please wait!

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:44.640
Can I ask you something?

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:47.600
Why did you leave the restaurant so suddenly?

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:48.850
Well...

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.270
That restaurant's steak is really delicious.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.990
We have already made sure the store is really clean.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.950
That's not it.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:04.700
I just felt a chill when I walked in, that's all. That's why...

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:09.120
S-So you're saying that there is a ghost or something like that in the restaurant?

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.510
That's not the right way to put it.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:13.020
In any case, I'm sorry.

00:10:13.020 --> 00:10:13.820
Hey.

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:15.260
What a stubborn customer.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.760
Maybe this had something to do with that cat-like sound...

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:25.370
When I carried Kanae-chan into the restaurant this afternoon, I thought I heard the meow of a cat.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.930
I also felt a chill then.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.900
S-So there really is a ghost...

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:35.210
But Kanae-chan's family got hurt one by one, and the restaurant's business went bad.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:36.690
Maybe those things had something to do with this.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.650
I get the same feelin' too.

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.130
We should go investigate.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.030
Okay.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:07.630
I heard the cat's meow at the same place where that customer was.

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:09.440
Right when I entered the restaurant.

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:13.440
Hadzuki-chan, what's wrong?

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:16.610
Cat! Cat! Cat! Cat! Cat! Cat! Cat! Cat! Cat! Cat! Cat!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.660
Hadzuki-chan, what're ya afraid of?

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:21.560
It's just a beckoning cat, it won't make a sound.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:33.290
I'm so lucky! Now I don't gotta buy a new one!

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.460
Wait!

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.420
That's so weird, Ai-chan!

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:39.920
Yeah, it didn't make a sound as it hit the ground!

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:41.380
Hey, yer right.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:44.850
This thing looks dark and kinda creepy.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.350
A beckoning cat?

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:49.060
Ah, the one Papa got from someone he knew.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.520
How long ago was that?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.840
About 10 days ago, I think.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:54.480
Someone from a store that was going out of business gave it to him.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:55.970
10 days ago...

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:57.860
Wasn't that when the thief broke in?

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.180
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:03.490
I told Papa that day that the beckoning cat even beckoned thieves.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.750
I knew it.

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:09.080
Yeah, it was from an antique shop over at the next town, called Limelight.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.750
But it's out of business now.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:14.320
Mister, we're going out for a bit.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:15.710
Ah, hey, wait!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:33.190
Pretty Witchy Aiko-chi!

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:36.600
Pretty Witchy Hadzuki-chi!

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:40.440
Pretty Witchy Doremi-chi!

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.870
Let's go!

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:47.370
Hey, ain't that the store?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.820
Ah, it is.

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:50.900
But didn't it go outta business?

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:51.830
That's strange.

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:56.850
That beckoning cat was brought here by a company that went bankrupt.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:58.250
Bankrupt?

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.760
Um, didn't this store go out of business?

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.190
That was going to happen...

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:12.440
We wish to use this to buy that furniture over there, that vase over there, and that painting too.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:15.300
What.

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:18.160
This store is positively wonderful.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:20.910
I have many friends who are into antiques.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:24.500
I'll be sure to recommend this store to them.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:26.500
Huh.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:32.160
Afterwards, that guy's friends kept buying stuff from my store.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:36.750
So, did this all happen after ya gave that beckoning cat to Kanae-chan's father?

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.710
Oh yeah, that's right.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:43.350
Just as I thought, that beckoning cat is the cause of all this misfortune.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.220
I wouldn't have thought that this thing was unlucky.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.570
Mister, we want to investigate further.

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:52.660
Can we take this home with us?

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.260
Sure, I don't mind.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.520
Majo Rika!

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:01.830
Welcome back.

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:03.110
Finished your part-time job already?

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.460
Majo Rika!

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:07.070
What happened? There's nothin' here!

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:10.030
I sold it all. How about that?

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:11.370
No way!

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:16.040
Pop's boyfriends are all rich lads.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:20.790
They brought their families here and bought everything in an instant!

00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:25.840
We earned so much that we even had Dela bring over a shaved ice machine.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:30.690
Pop has such nice boyfriends.

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:32.600
She's much more reliable than you three.

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.640
No way!

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:38.560
What's wrong with that beckoning cat?

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:40.950
It was at our friend's house.

00:14:40.950 --> 00:14:41.960
Let me see that.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.400
I'm taking this back to the Witch World to have it checked out.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.030
Can you lend it to me?

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:48.880
Sure.

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:50.490
That's what we wanted to do anyway.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:52.080
Then I'll take this back with me.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.710
Why's she in such a hurry?

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:56.410
Who knows?

00:14:58.630 --> 00:14:59.960
What's wrong, Rere?

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.500
What's wrong?

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:08.310
Kanae-chan's restaurant suddenly got a lot of customers.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:10.250
There are people waiting in line outside!

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:10.890
No way!

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:12.890
There was no one there a minute ago!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.740
Anyway, let's go check it out.

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.600
Thank you all so much for today.

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.650
I've never had so many customers.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.950
It really was 'cause of that beckoning cat.

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:31.550
But they ran out of steak.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.160
I didn't get to eat any.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.530
Doremi-chan.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:37.110
Well then, Mister, we're going home now.

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:38.370
Okay, later!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.430
Thanks for your work, please come help out tomorrow.

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:46.040
Ai-chan, I can definitely eat steak tomorrow, right?

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:47.670
Doremi-chan, yer brain is a steak.

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.430
Ah, that's...

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.440
The Queen's carriage!

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:16.330
I am here to pick you up by order of Her Majesty.

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:19.700
Now, please board the carriage.

00:16:31.420 --> 00:16:33.190
So pretty...

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:35.210
I've always wanted to ride in one of these.

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.390
It's so beautiful.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:52.820
So what's goin' on?

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:55.910
That beckoning cat is an unbelievable item.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.700
Unbelievable item?

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:00.580
Her Majesty arrives!

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:14.550
So she's the Queen of the Witch World?

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:19.320
The three of you, thank you for coming.

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:21.130
Now, please rise.

00:17:23.310 --> 00:17:30.770
That beckoning cat you found is a Bad Item that had been missing for quite some time.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.530
Bad Item?

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.990
Dela, please explain.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:36.820
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:43.770
Okay, about 1,000 years ago, you could go freely between the Witch World and the Human World.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:47.830
During that time, witches and humans lived in harmony.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:53.760
But there was an evil wizard who secretly took the Bad Cards, cards which possess a great evil magic,

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:58.550
from their sealed location in the Witch World to the Human World.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:02.680
These Bad Cards were then sealed in various items in the Human World,

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:06.560
turning them into Bad Items, bringing great misfortune to the humans.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:10.610
The humans then came to hate witches as a result.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:13.480
So, we cut off communications.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:23.320
We caught the evil wizard, but a number of these Bad Items remain in the Human World.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.290
So that beckoning cat was...

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:27.300
Yes.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:31.660
A Bad Item will grant you the opposite of what you wish for.

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:34.590
They are very fearsome items.

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:40.550
So what was originally used to lure customers in and keep the family safe ended up hurtin' Kanae-chan and her family.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.310
You three.

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:44.010
Please show your Certificates.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.590
Certificates?

00:18:45.590 --> 00:18:47.790
Doremi-chan, have you given them to them?

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:49.860
I completely forgot.

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:52.050
Here they are. One for you, and one for you.

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.240
It changed color.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:04.200
Now you girls are the Pureleine.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.160
Pureleine?

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:08.320
You found a Bad Item and refrained from using it.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:12.760
Furthermore, you possess pure and kind hearts.

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:14.540
That is why I confer unto you that title.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:20.130
The Pureleine can extract the Bad Cards from the Bad Items.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.600
Majo Rin, bring over the beckoning cat.

00:19:22.600 --> 00:19:23.230
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:30.640
Now we want you to extract the Bad Card from this beckoning cat.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:32.100
How do we do that?

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:37.080
By using Magical Stage and then saying "Come out, Bad Card!"

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:38.570
Now, please try it.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:39.790
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.890
Pirika Pirilala Carefreely!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:52.220
Paipai Ponpoi Flexibly!

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:57.790
Pameruku Laruku Proudly!

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:10.550
Magical Stage!

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:18.820
Come out, Bad Card!

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:30.810
Magnificent.

00:20:33.650 --> 00:20:35.670
Your Majesty, what do we do with this now?

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:41.590
This is the Pureleine Computer.

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:45.240
Please insert the Card into it.

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:00.270
Doremi-chan,

00:21:00.270 --> 00:21:01.480
Hadzuki-chan,

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:03.110
Aiko-chan.

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:08.070
From now on, as the Pureleine, please collect the Bad Cards.

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.870
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:16.160
Doremi-chan, Hadzuki-chan, Ai-chan!

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:19.090
Kanae-chan, is your foot alright?

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:23.190
Yes, it's really unbelievable. It stopped hurting all of a sudden.

00:21:23.190 --> 00:21:25.130
It's 'cause we took out the Bad Card!

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:27.090
Ah, it's nothin'! Don't mind me!

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:32.520
And they also caught the thief, so we got our things back.

00:21:32.520 --> 00:21:35.760
Mama got well and was discharged a month ahead of schedule.

00:21:35.760 --> 00:21:37.760
Things are going great!

00:21:37.760 --> 00:21:39.360
I see, thank goodness!

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:42.750
Hey, wait! So what does this mean about our part-time job!?

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:45.040
Mama is back, so we're fine now.

00:21:45.040 --> 00:21:46.950
Papa told me to thank you.

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:49.000
No way!

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:52.390
What about my steak?

00:21:52.390 --> 00:21:57.370
I really am the world's unluckiest pretty girl!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:05.650
Wow, the Queen gave us the Pureleine computer!

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:08.090
Now we can easily find the Bad Items!

00:22:08.090 --> 00:22:10.260
I don't think it'll be too hard!

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:12.120
Okay, let's try it out!

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:15.250
Eh? There's someone in the computer!

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:16.680
It looks like a Witch Frog.

00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:17.970
Let's have a drink.

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:18.720
Don't tell me...

00:22:18.720 --> 00:22:19.600
No way...

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:21.020
Right?

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:22.360
Oyaji!?

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:24.220
Ojamajo Doremi!

00:22:24.220 --> 00:22:25.820
The Arrival of Oyajiide!?

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:25.830
Happy! Lucky! For all of you!
The Arrival of Oyajiide!?

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:28.670
Happy! Lucky! For all of you!
